== 9.7 Chapter 9 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [The functional unit of the kidney is the],
  [villus],
  [neurone],
  [nephron],
  [alveolus]
)

#mcq(2, [Urea is formed in the],
  [liver],
  [skin],
  [bladder],
  [kidney]
)

#mcq(3, [The process by which glucose is returned to the blood from the kidney tubule is],
  [deamination],
  [selective reabsorption],
  [ultrafiltration],
  [osmoregulation]
)

#mcq(4, [Homeostasis is best defined as],
  [the removal of waste products],
  [the control of body movement],
  [the maintenance of a constant internal environment],
  [the digestion of food]
)

#mcq(5, [Which of these is an excretory organ?],
  [Small intestine],
  [Stomach],
  [Pancreas],
  [Kidney]
)

#mcq(6, [Ultrafiltration in the glomerulus is driven by],
  [blood pressure],
  [active transport],
  [osmosis],
  [diffusion of water]
)

#mcq(7, [Which substance would *not* be found in normal urine?],
  [Water],
  [Urea],
  [Excess salts],
  [Glucose]
)

#mcq(8, [The sweat glands of the skin help to],
  [cool the body and excrete salts],
  [make vitamin D],
  [digest fat],
  [store fat]
)

#mcq(9, [When the body is too cold, the blood vessels in the skin],
  [dilate],
  [constrict],
  [do not change],
